00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:04.160
So here,

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:09.600
xi is an input called a feature

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:13.820
outputs is

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:18.060
a predicted

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:21.340
yi value,

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:23.440
OK?

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:28.140
And there were two formats of
hypothesis functions, or two

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:33.160
types of hypothesis functions,
that we proposed on Tuesday.

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:35.640
What were the two?

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:36.900
Yes, and remind me of your name?

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:37.900
Maj.
Maj.

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:39.940
Near and constant.

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:41.600
Good, the first one,

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:46.770
and the one that we will spend
all of our time on today

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:48.740
was the constant model.

00:08:48.740 --> 00:08:54.740
So let me bring this to the next
page.

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:03.420
The constant model,

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:05.900
the formula looks a little funny

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:09.760
because it says h of xi on the
left,

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:11.580
